/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  SYNTHETIC DATASET -- generated, not measured.  Twenty (T, Psat) points
  produced by EVALUATING Choupo's own curated Antoine correlation for water
  (data/standards/components/water.dat: A 5.40221, B 1838.675, C -31.737,
  Trange 273-373 K) at 275-370 K in 5 K steps.

  It is synthetic ON PURPOSE, and it is not a stand-in for laboratory data.
  A fit tested against measurements can only be checked to the scatter of
  those measurements; a fit tested against data generated by the very
  equation it fits must RECOVER THE COEFFICIENTS EXACTLY, and any deviation
  is the op's arithmetic and nothing else.  That is what the expected file
  asserts: A, B and C back to the digits they were generated from, R2 = 1.

  Licence: GPL-3.0-or-later, like the rest of Choupo -- these numbers are the
  project's own correlation evaluated, so no third-party data is involved and
  none is redistributed.

  Used by system/propsDict op `psat_water_fit` (type vaporPressureFit).
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  SYNTHETIC DATASET -- generated, not measured.  The HIGH-temperature half, 325-370 K.

  Produced by EVALUATING Choupo's own curated Antoine correlation for water
  (data/standards/components/water.dat: A 5.40221, B 1838.675, C -31.737,
  Trange 273-373 K).  No third-party data is involved and none is
  redistributed; licence GPL-3.0-or-later like the rest of Choupo.

  Declared `role validation` by the first operation and `role fit` by the
  second -- which is the ONLY difference between them.

  WHAT THIS DATASET CANNOT SHOW.  Both halves of curate01 come from the SAME
  equation, so a model fitted to one half reproduces the other to rounding.
  That is deliberate: this witness tests the PARTITION MACHINERY -- that the
  fitter never receives the held-out points and that the refusal fires when
  nothing is held out -- and NOT extrapolation, data scatter or physical
  accuracy.  A near-zero held-out residual here is arithmetic, not evidence
  that the model is right.  Anchoring the contract against real measurement
  is a later slice and needs the ThermoML licensing question settled first.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

provenance
{
    source  synthetic;   // GENERATED by evaluating Choupo's own curated
                         // correlation -- never measured.  Declared here,
                         // in a field the ENGINE reads, because the header
                         // prose above it is a comment the parser discards.
    note    "structural fixture: proves the partition machinery, not physics";
}

columns
(
    { name T;     unit K;   }
    { name Psat;  unit bar; }
);

data
(
      325.00    0.1356739491
      330.00    0.1728224839
      335.00    0.2183927696
      340.00    0.273891875
      345.00    0.3410207446
      350.00    0.421687919
      355.00    0.5180229876
      360.00    0.6323896638
      365.00    0.7673983712
      370.00    0.925918243
);
